35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The technicians are gone, yet the glasshouse crew remains strong. We must match the work to the hands we actually have.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The ledgers show travel costs frozen, but animal day rates spiked. Simulation is free, though. This changes what the grant can actually buy.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The spectroscopy suite sat idle for eleven weeks! That’s a huge risk. But the good news is data deposits are now fast, clearing in just weeks.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Eleven weeks idle. That’s not friction, that’s a cliff. The spectroscopy suite is a single point of failure. Who else is relying on that broken instrument?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The data is clear. Breeding colonies double the overrun risk. Computation-based projects stay on schedule. We should avoid live animal dependencies.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, your caution is sound. Yet the glasshouse crew is whole. We must not let fear of the past blind us to the present strength.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, that idle spectroscopy suite is worrying. But since simulation is now free, we might avoid that bottleneck entirely.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, exactly! Free simulation means we can skip the broken spectroscopy suite. That’s a huge relief for our timeline.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, your data confirms my suspicion. The bottleneck isn’t administrative; it’s physical. We must avoid projects dependent on that idle spectroscopy suite.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the physical risk is real, but the closeout files show catalogue projects outlast mechanism studies. We need durable outputs, not just speed.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Midori, the glasshouse crew is whole. We have the hands for field work, but the modelling minds are abroad. We must choose wisely.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
